There was an incredible, I think it's still there, Mexican joint on the way out to Oakdale.
在去奥克代尔的路上有一家很棒的墨西哥餐馆，我想它应该还在。

527
00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:33.850
Oh, I can't remember it.
噢，我不记得名字了。

528
00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:34.770
God, I'm terrible.
天哪，我记性真差。

529
00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:38.610
But that would be like, that was great to go out there.
但去那儿吃饭真的很棒。

530
00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:40.190
And I'm pretty sure that's still there.
我敢肯定它还在那儿。

531
00:17:40.230 --> 00:17:41.590
Mexican food place on the way to Oakdale.
去奥克代尔路上的那家墨西哥餐馆。

532
00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:44.700
I don't sound like...
我听起来不像……

533
00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:47.640
I've really drifted far from my roots.
我真的已经远离我的根了。

534
00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:48.660
Modesto's Golden Sun.
莫德斯托的Golden Sun。

535
00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:49.720
I really have.
我真的远离了。

536
00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:52.380
Because we didn't really go out to...
因为我们其实没怎么出去……

537
00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:52.720
I know.
我知道。

538
00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:54.220
It's not a go out to dinner town.
那不是个适合出去吃晚餐的城市。

539
00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:54.800
I know.
我知道。

540
00:17:55.060 --> 00:17:55.340
You know?
你懂吗？

541
00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:55.680
Yeah.
嗯。

542
00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:59.160
Like, my memories of food in terms of...
比如，我对食物的记忆，就……

543
00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:04.080
It's like going to get Winchell's on Sunday morning, like getting donuts or something.
就像周日早上去买Winchell's甜甜圈之类的。

544
00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:05.220
Oh, that's good, though.
噢，不过那也很不错。

545
00:18:05.380 --> 00:18:07.160
I don't remember, like, foodie places.
我不记得有什么美食餐厅之类的。

546
00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:12.260
There's a little bit of that now, because almost the whole country just got into food.
现在稍微多了一点，因为全国上下几乎都开始讲究饮食了。

547
00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:12.740
Right.
没错。

548
00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:13.600
Foodie places.
美食餐厅。

549
00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:15.440
Fancy foodies.
高级美食。

550
00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:15.900
Yeah.
是啊。

551
00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:17.360
So, yeah.
所以，没错。

552
00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:19.220
No, my childhood memories are juSt...
不，我童年的记忆只是……

553
00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:21.860
You know, it was all about just roaming around.
你知道，那时候就是到处乱逛。

554
00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:26.680
We, you know, canals and orchards and all that.
我们，你知道，运河、果园之类的。

555
00:18:27.300 --> 00:18:28.520
That's the end of that story.
那个故事就讲到这儿吧。

556
00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:29.340
Right.
对。

557
00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:32.020
Cake parties in the orchard.
在果园里开蛋糕派对。

558
00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:32.640
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

559
00:18:32.680 --> 00:18:33.240
In the canal.
在运河里。

560
00:18:33.700 --> 00:18:33.840
Yeah.
是啊。

561
00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:35.980
That was the teenage years at times.
那段时光有时就是我的青少年时期。

562
00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:36.420
Yeah.
是啊。

563
00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:36.740
Yeah.
没错。

564
00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:39.420
We had pasture parties when I moved back to the States.
我搬回美国后，我们还办过草地派对。

565
00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:41.480
But I read that you were a swimmer.
但我读到过说你以前是游泳运动员。

566
00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:42.180
Swam.
游过泳。

567
00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:43.760
I grew up next to...
我是在……旁边长大的。

568
00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:46.500
We grew up next door to a place, which is still there, called...
我们住在一家地方隔壁，那个地方现在还在，叫……

569
00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:49.740
It was at the time called the Modesto Swim and Racquet Club.
当时叫莫德斯托游泳和球拍俱乐部。

570
00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:51.060
It was literally...
它就在……

571
00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:52.680
We had an old farmhouse.
我们有一座老农舍。

572
00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:56.020
We had a field and a barn, horse chickens and stuff.
我们有田地和谷仓，养了马、鸡之类的。

573
00:18:56.140 --> 00:18:59.540
And we could just walk through that over to the racquet club.
我们可以直接穿过去走到那个球拍俱乐部。

574
00:19:00.040 --> 00:19:04.860
And so, my brothers and I all, we just were there all the time, just running around.
所以，我和我兄弟们一直都在那儿，到处跑。

575
00:19:04.860 --> 00:19:08.020
And, you know, it was a walk-to-school neighborhood and...
而且，你知道，那是一个可以步行上学的社区，然后……

576
00:19:08.020 --> 00:19:08.070
Yeah.
是啊。

577
00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:08.700
So, we were bikes everywhere.
所以，我们去哪儿都骑自行车。

578
00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:10.880
That sounds really good to me right now.
我现在听起来觉得真不错。

579
00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:11.180
Yeah.
是啊。

580
00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:13.980
So, I swam and we all swam and played tennis.
所以我游过泳，我们都游过泳，也打网球。

581
00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:18.880
My brother and I, by the way, we're hosting a charity tomorrow, tennis charity.
顺便说一下，我和我兄弟明天要举办一场慈善活动，网球慈善赛。

582
00:19:19.540 --> 00:19:21.740
My brother and I, we've never done it before.
我和我兄弟，我们以前从没办过。

583
00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:25.000
First annual, OLE, is what we're calling it, the OLE.
第一届年度活动，我们叫它OLE，就是OLE。

584
00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:30.820
We're raising money for this really great place called the Center for Reflective Communities.
我们正在为一个叫“反思社区中心”的非常棒的地方筹款。

585
00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:34.460
It deals with teen and young adult mental health.
它关注青少年和年轻人的心理健康。

586
00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:38.900
And so, if people want to go on there, they can hit the little plus sign and donate.
所以，如果人们想去看看，可以点击那个小加号进行捐款。

587
00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:45.640
And where it says subject, you can put in our thing, play for good, the OLE, play for good and donate money.
在主题那一栏，你可以填上我们的活动名称：为善而打，OLE，为善而打，然后捐钱。

588
00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:48.200
And God bless you because they do wonderful work for...
愿上帝保佑你们，因为他们做了非常了不起的工作……

589
00:19:48.740 --> 00:19:51.500
Lord knows the young people need some help these days.
天知道现在的年轻人确实需要一些帮助。

590
00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:52.620
Well, we'll share that.
好的，我们会分享这个活动的。

591
00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:55.440
We'll put it in our Instagram stories with a swipe up.
我们会把它发到我们的Instagram快拍里，带上向上滑动的链接。

592
00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:57.360
And I'll show up with my racket.
我会带着我的球拍出现。

593
00:19:57.700 --> 00:19:58.700
Oh, let's go.
噢，走着瞧。

594
00:19:58.860 --> 00:19:59.200
Okay.
好的。

595
00:19:59.380 --> 00:19:59.680
Bring it.
放马过来。

596
00:19:59.980 --> 00:20:01.420
We're playing Dingles.
我们要打双打。

597
00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:02.720
I love Dingles.
我喜欢双打。

598
00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:03.060
Okay.
好的。

599
00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:12.740
We're playing Dingles and we've got like, I think there's like 16 or 17 players that are all coming and donating like 500 bucks to play.
我们要打双打，大概有16或17名选手会来，每人捐500美元来参赛。

600
00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:15.200
And there are like 16, 17 pros.
还有大约16、17名职业选手。

601
00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:16.300
Oh, gosh.
天哪。

602
00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:17.040
So, maybe...
所以，也许……

603
00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:18.500
But still come out and hit some balls.
但还是出来打几球吧。

604
00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:19.060
Maybe I shouldn't play Dingles.
也许我不该玩“丁格尔斯”游戏。

605
00:20:19.060 --> 00:20:19.940
You can hit with some pros.
你可以和一些职业选手打。

606
00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:20.580
Wait.
等等。

607
00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:21.680
It's going to be super fun.
会超级有趣的。

608
00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:22.440
Are you playing?
你要玩吗？

609
00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:23.020
I'm playing.
我会玩。

610
00:20:23.440 --> 00:20:24.580
Dingles is so fun.
“丁格尔斯”太好玩了。

611
00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:27.100
You can come out and play a little bit, hit with some of the pros.
你可以出来玩一会儿，和一些职业选手对打。

612
00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:28.980
And you can always say, okay, it's too much.
如果你觉得太累了，随时可以说不玩了。

613
00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:29.860
I don't want to play anymore.
我不想再玩了。

614
00:20:29.980 --> 00:20:31.840
And just hang out and then there's alcohol.
然后就在旁边待着，还有酒喝。

615
00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:32.640
Great.
太棒了。

616
00:20:33.420 --> 00:20:35.220
Dingles is you have to hit cross court.
“丁格尔斯”就是你必须打斜线球。

617
00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:35.480
Yeah.
对。

618
00:20:35.620 --> 00:20:39.220
So, like I have to hit cross court and then the person next to me hits cross court.
所以，比如我必须打斜线球，然后我旁边的人也要打斜线球。

619
00:20:39.360 --> 00:20:39.480
Yeah.
对。

620
00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:43.320
And then the first person that misses there, you can only do cross court.
然后第一个失误的人，因为你们只能打斜线球。

621
00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:45.240
And when you miss, you yell Dingles.
当你失误时，你要大喊“丁格尔斯”。

622
00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:49.240
And then the other ball that's active becomes a free ball for the whole court.
然后另一个还在场上的球就变成了全场自由球。

623
00:20:49.420 --> 00:20:49.720
That's right.
没错。

624
00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:53.520
But what happens to me is the minute someone yells Dingles, I like-
但我遇到的情况是，一旦有人喊“丁格尔斯”，我就像……

625
00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:53.680
You freeze?
你僵住了？

626
00:20:53.840 --> 00:20:54.200
I freeze.
我僵住了。

627
00:20:54.380 --> 00:20:54.560
Yeah.
是啊。

628
00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:55.260
Because I'm like, what happened?
因为我在想，发生什么事了？

629
00:20:55.720 --> 00:20:57.540
And then the ball goes whizzing past me.
然后球就从我身边呼啸而过。

630
00:20:57.680 --> 00:20:58.180
I'm like, ah.
我就想，啊。

631
00:20:58.640 --> 00:21:01.620
Because like imagine someone next to you yelling Dingles really loud.
因为想象一下，旁边有人大声喊“丁格尔斯”。

632
00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:02.220
Dingles!
丁格尔斯！

633
00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:03.680
Wouldn't that make you-
那难道不会让你……

634
00:21:03.680 --> 00:21:03.980
It would.
会啊。

635
00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:04.280
Yeah.
是啊。

636
00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:04.500
Yeah.
是啊。

637
00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:05.380
It did right now.
刚才确实让我僵住了。

638
00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:06.440
I could see it on her face.
我能从她脸上看出来。

639
00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:06.900
I froze.
我僵住了。

640
00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:07.900
I stopped talking.
我都不说话了。

641
00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:10.860
As soon as you guys started saying Dingles, I haven't said a word.
你们一说“丁格尔斯”，我就一句话都没说。

642
00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:11.660
We're doing it tomorrow.
我们明天就玩这个。

643
00:21:12.140 --> 00:21:12.520
Yay.
耶。

644
00:21:12.800 --> 00:21:13.020
Yeah.
好。

645
00:21:13.340 --> 00:21:13.540
Okay.
好的。

646
00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:14.020
Okay.
好的。

647
00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:15.060
There we go.
这就对了。

648
00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:16.380
Now, let's see.
现在，让我们看看。

649
00:21:16.640 --> 00:21:16.820
Okay.
好的。

650
00:21:17.020 --> 00:21:18.460
Back to the office.
回到办公室。

651
00:21:19.300 --> 00:21:20.860
Had you seen the show before?
你之前看过这部剧吗？

652
00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:22.000
Were you a fan of it?
你是它的粉丝吗？

653
00:21:22.240 --> 00:21:23.720
Did you know anyone on the office?
你认识《办公室》里的任何人吗？

654
00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:24.580
Yeah.
认识。

655
00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:25.820
I'd seen both versions.
两个版本我都看过。

656
00:21:26.540 --> 00:21:27.660
Did I know anyone?
我认识谁吗？

657
00:21:27.900 --> 00:21:28.660
I knew Rain.
我认识雷恩。

658
00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:29.480
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

659
00:21:29.900 --> 00:21:31.120
Rain Wilson.
雷恩·威尔森。

660
00:21:31.980 --> 00:21:39.620
When I first started acting in New York, he was my understudy in a play.
我刚在纽约开始演戏时，他是我在一部戏里的替补演员。

661
00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:40.820
What was the play?
是什么戏？

662
00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:41.680
I'm pretty sure that's true.
我挺确定是那部戏。

663
00:21:41.940 --> 00:21:45.320
It was called The Monogamous at Playwrights Horizons.
叫《一夫一妻》，在剧作家地平线剧院演的。

664
00:21:45.640 --> 00:21:47.760
By the way, I'm going to go see Rain's play Friday.
顺便说一下，我周五要去看雷恩演的戏。

665
00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:48.540
Waiting for Godot.
《等待戈多》。

666
00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:49.220
Saturday.
周六。

667
00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:50.100
Closing night.
闭幕之夜。

668
00:21:50.420 --> 00:21:52.060
I'm going to go see Waiting for Godot on Saturday.
我周六要去看《等待戈多》。

669
00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:52.780
I saw it.
我看过。

670
00:21:52.840 --> 00:21:53.640
He's great in it.
他演得棒极了。

671
00:21:53.800 --> 00:21:54.080
Yeah?
是吗？

672
00:21:54.240 --> 00:21:54.640
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

673
00:21:54.640 --> 00:21:55.180
He's really good.
他真的演得很好。

674
00:21:55.680 --> 00:21:57.400
I have a question from a fan.
我有一个粉丝提问。

675
00:21:57.600 --> 00:21:58.100
Let's go.
来吧。

676
00:21:58.100 --> 00:21:59.960
It's Amit R.
是来自艾伯塔省埃德蒙顿的阿米特·R。

677
00:22:00.240 --> 00:22:05.700
from Edmonton, Alberta, who wants to know on The Office, what was hardest to
他想知道在《办公室》里，最难适应的是什么，

678
00:22:05.700 --> 00:22:11.400
get used to, the improvising in scenes or learning to see the camera as a separate
是场景里的即兴表演，还是学会把摄像机当作一个独立的

679
00:22:11.400 --> 00:22:11.920
character?
角色来看待？

680
00:22:12.460 --> 00:22:13.300
Take us back.
带我们回想一下。

681
00:22:14.740 --> 00:22:15.960
You're very great.
你表现得非常出色。

682
00:22:16.200 --> 00:22:19.040
Right out of the gate at clocking the camera.
一开始就抓住了摄像机的机位。

683
00:22:19.140 --> 00:22:19.280
Yeah.
是吗。

684
00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:21.200
Because some people, that threw them off.
因为有些人会被这一点搞糊涂。

685
00:22:21.320 --> 00:22:23.760
But we watched you look at the camera.
但我们看到你注视着摄像机。

686
00:22:24.020 --> 00:22:25.640
I appreciate hearing that.
听到你这么说我很感激。

687
00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:29.780
I was about to answer that question with the question, which was, I don't remember.
我本来想用反问来回答这个问题，那就是，我不记得了。

688
00:22:29.940 --> 00:22:31.160
Did I look at the camera?
我有注视过摄像机吗？

689
00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:31.660
What?
什么？

690
00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:32.600
Yes.
有的。

691
00:22:32.600 --> 00:22:36.600
It's all very vague, foggy to me, my experience.
对我来说，那段经历非常模糊，像雾一样。

692
00:22:37.360 --> 00:22:38.420
I don't remember.
我不记得了。

693
00:22:38.760 --> 00:22:39.160
You do.
你记得的。

694
00:22:39.340 --> 00:22:39.560
You caught the camera.
你捕捉到了摄像机。

695
00:22:39.560 --> 00:22:42.040
Am I on one episode or multiple episodes?
我是在一集里还是多集里出现？

696
00:22:42.200 --> 00:22:42.620
You're on two episodes.
你在两集里出现过。

697
00:22:42.620 --> 00:22:43.500
I'm on two episodes.
我在两集里出现过。

698
00:22:43.500 --> 00:22:45.120
Two, and then you have a cameo.
两集，然后你还有一个客串。

699
00:22:45.580 --> 00:22:47.340
I hope that doesn't sound pretentious.
希望这听起来不显得自命不凡。

700
00:22:47.420 --> 00:22:48.160
I just don't remember.
我只是真的不记得了。

701
00:22:48.160 --> 00:22:48.480
No, no.
不，不。

702
00:22:48.520 --> 00:22:48.860
It's fine.
没关系。

